<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alcibiades</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 450–<a href="/years/404-bce">404 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alcibiades was an Athenian statesman and general and an associate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/socrates">Socrates</a>. He promoted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicilian-expedition">Sicilian Expedition</a> of 415 BCE, deserted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> when accused of sacrilege, and later returned to lead the Athenian fleet to victories such as Cyzicus in 410 BCE. Exiled again after the defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/notion-ancient-city">Notium</a>, he was murdered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phrygia">Phrygia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alcibiades.jpg" alt="Alcibiades" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: François-André Vincent · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Detail_of_Alcibiades_from_Alcibiades_Being_Taught_by_Socrates_(1776)_by_Fran%C3%A7ois-Andr%C3%A9_Vincent.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
